@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
' purpose: the chosen difficulty is persisted and restored on the next enter — picking it every game is the bug
' status: proposed 2026-09-17, not implemented; _spec/_plans/ is exempt from the SPEC-reference rule.
' would touch: not in this tree — no difficulty enum or persist key exists under
'   the sandbox checkout (measured 2026-09-17). Locate the owning UI and
'   persist modules before a covers: line can be honest.
'   the picker primitive ................ _spec/_plans/chess-ui-primitives.puml
'   the journey beat .................... _spec/_plans/chess-user-journey.puml
'   the export that should copy it ...... _spec/_plans/game-export-localstorage.puml
' Notes are capped at 5 lines x 50 columns; one idea per anchor.
'
' ── WHAT THE LINE ITEM SETTLES ─────────────────────────────────────────────
' "save difficulty selection" is a PERSISTENCE beat on the journey. The player
' picks a difficulty, the pick is stored, the next enter restores it. A default
' that ignores last time is the defect.
'
' ── WHAT IT DOES NOT SETTLE ────────────────────────────────────────────────
'   the enum (easy / normal / hard, or a rating)
'   localStorage vs account
'   whether a match in progress may change difficulty mid-game
'
' Saving only in memory dies on refresh. Saving a second copy that export
' does not read will disagree in bug dumps.
title PLANNED — last difficulty is restored on enter;\na forgotten pick is the defect

component "difficulty picker" as PICK <<app>>
component "persist key" as KEY <<db>>
component "next enter restores" as REST <<app>>
component "**in-memory only**\nrefresh forgets the pick" as MEM <<error>>
component "game export blob" as EX <<app>>
component "localStorage live game" as LS <<db>>

PICK ARROW_MAIN KEY
KEY ARROW_MAIN REST
REST ARROW_MAIN PICK : default = last
PICK ARROW_ERROR MEM
KEY ARROW_MAIN EX
LS ARROW_OPTIONAL KEY

note bottom of MEM
  **An in-memory variable is not a save, because a
  refresh makes the player reselect difficulty
  every session.** The persistence key has to
  outlive the browser tab.
end note

note bottom of KEY
  **One persistence key has two readers: the
  journey restores from it and export copies it.**
  A third encoding inside the game blob is how
  dumps disagree with the picker.
end note

note right of PICK
  **The shared picker is the control, including
  for analytics and tutorial gates.** Do not draw
  a second difficulty widget that can drift from
  the saved enumeration.
end note

legend bottom
  **The order to do it in**
  ==
  **1. Name the enum and the key.** What values exist today, where a pick is
  stored if at all. If it is already in the game blob, restore from there
  instead of adding a parallel key.
  --
  **2. Write on confirm, read on enter.** Picker uses the primitive kit.
  Changing mid-game is out of scope until a test names it.
  ==
  **3. Include it in export.** The dump of a game names the difficulty it
  was played at. Analytics can group on that field later.
  --
  **Left open**: per-mode vs global; account sync; whether tutorial difficulty
  is a separate key.
end legend
@enduml
